"""A2A server for the "{{agentName}}" agent (generated by genproj).

Run it with:

    uvicorn agent.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port {{listenPort}}

The A2A app, agent card and JSON-RPC transport come from the official A2A
Python SDK (`a2a-sdk`); this module wires a Pydantic AI agent into it as an
`AgentExecutor`. The served card's advertised JSON-RPC dialect and the dialect
the endpoint actually accepts both come from `SUPPORTED_DIALECTS` / `PROTOCOL_VERSION`
below, so the card can never claim a dialect this server rejects - the defect
that made every FastA2A-generated agent undialable.

Serve with the same SDK the caller uses: the LiteLLM gateway invokes this agent
with an `a2a-sdk` client, so using `a2a-sdk`'s server removes the client/server
skew by construction instead of papering over it.{{agentRegisterModuleDoc}}

The task store is the agent's own conversation state on disk (agent/history.py):
A2A groups turns by `contextId` and keeps each turn's messages, so that state is
the transcript roost's History panel reads. It is persisted in SQLite under
`$AGENT_STATE_DIR`, so history survives a restart instead of being lost with the
SDK's default in-memory store.

Bind 0.0.0.0, not 127.0.0.1: the caller is the LiteLLM proxy reaching this
container across the network, so a loopback bind is unreachable.
"""

